MyGo patch 0009 (VoxtNew): Tester.AccessLabels and Tester.ClickControl,
so that a test can check what assistive technology reaches and click a
control by its label.

A Tester never turned assistive technology on, so a test could not tell
whether VoiceOver reaches a control: one inside a button does not (a
button is a leaf to assistive technology), as VoxtNew's Test button on a
remote service's card did not. AccessLabels turns it on, as VoiceOver
reading the window would, runs a frame and returns the labels of the
elements it sees. ClickControl clicks the element of a label that can be
pressed: a switch, not the row title beside it that shares its label,
which Click finds first. TestAccessLabels, TestClickControl.

